  "html": "<h1>Encoded Doc Links</h1>\n<p>A link destination is a URL, so a sibling whose filename contains a space has to be percent-encoded to be linked at all. This is the spelling editors and previews produce, and it must resolve to the same page as the angle-bracket form below:</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://wiki.example.net/wiki/spaces/ENG/pages/4343/My+Sibling+Page\">percent-encoded</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://wiki.example.net/wiki/spaces/ENG/pages/4343/My+Sibling+Page\">angle brackets</a></p>\n<p>A bare space is not a valid destination, so this is not a link at all and stays literal text -- the same as GitHub and a local preview render it:</p>\n<p>[bare space](my sibling.md)</p>\n<p>The fragment is a URL too. An encoded anchor has to be decoded before it can be matched against a heading slug, which is Unicode-aware:</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://wiki.example.net/wiki/spaces/ENG/pages/4344/Plain+Sibling#Café-Section\">encoded fragment</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://wiki.example.net/wiki/spaces/ENG/pages/4344/Plain+Sibling#Café-Section\">literal fragment</a></p>\n<p>A same-page anchor takes the same path through the anchor map:</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://wiki.example.net/wiki/spaces/ENG/pages/4345/Encoded+Doc+Links#Café-Section\">same page, encoded</a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://wiki.example.net/wiki/spaces/ENG/pages/4345/Encoded+Doc+Links#Café-Section\">same page, literal</a></p>\n<p>Both halves at once -- encoded filename and encoded fragment:</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://wiki.example.net/wiki/spaces/ENG/pages/4343/My+Sibling+Page#Café-Section\">both encoded</a></p>\n<p>A sibling that is not in this set is Broken; the reported message still echoes the destination as written, encoding and all, rather than a resolved answer:</p>\n<p>LINK BROKEN: nosuch%20file.md (not found)</p>\n<p>An absolute URL keeps its encoding untouched:</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://example.net/a%20b.md\">external</a></p>\n<h2>Café Section</h2>\n<p>Content under a heading whose slug is not ASCII.</p>\n",
  "warnings": []
}
